  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">SCLR Phase 3, Year 2</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project primary goal is to support grassroots community organizations (CBOs) and self-help groups (SHGs) within communities affected by climate disruptions and other recurring anthropogenic challenges.
The project objective is to utilize the SCLR approach to deliver rapid, effective, efficient, responsible, and coordinated emergency relief interventions to the most vulnerable in Fort-Libert&#xE9; commune, Nord-East department of Haiti. This initiative aims to address immediate needs and enhance community preparedness and resilience against future disasters.
The project aims to directly assist at least 100 vulnerable families, comprising approximately 500 individuals, by providing direct funding to CBOs/Self-Help Groups for the implementation of their priority initiatives within their respective communities.
Identified vulnerable and marginalized groups include people living with disabilities, single mothers, older individuals lacking family support, and families living below the poverty line.</narrative>
  </description>
